CREATED:20260224T160415Z
DESCRIPTION:This symposium will bring the School of Medicine and the broad
 er community together for conversations at the intersection of science an
 d culture. Featuring keynote speaker <a href="https://www.med.unc.edu/mic
 roimm/people/rebekah-layton-phd-cmc-pcc/">Rebekah Layton\, PhD\, CMC\, PC
 C\,</a> associate chair of education and training in the Department of Mi
 crobiology and Immunology at UNC-Chapel Hill. The theme of her talk is "C
 areer development\, mentoring\, and wellness: Setting the stage for gradu
 ate and postdoctoral trainee success." The symposium will be sponsored by
  the Office for Culture\, Engagement\, and Impact and The Office for Facu
 lty. <a href="https://oedi.wufoo.com/forms/zy6uqgo1hdyyqb/">Register here
 .</a>
DURATION:PT3H
